# ABAP Project Conventions (always-on)

This is an **SAP ECC / S/4HANA ABAP** project. The current initiative is a
**read-only integrated operations monitoring** program (SM37 / ST22 / SXI_MONITOR).
These conventions are always in effect. On-demand playbooks live in `.cursor/skills/`
— consult them and apply their techniques automatically during implementation,
review, refactoring, and documentation.

## Non-negotiable invariants

- **Read-only.** No `INSERT / UPDATE / MODIFY / DELETE`, no `COMMIT WORK` /
  `ROLLBACK` (for business intent), no `ENQUEUE_* / DEQUEUE_*`, no update task
  (`CALL FUNCTION ... IN UPDATE TASK`), and no state-changing BAPIs/FMs
  (job re-run, message re-send, etc.). Drill-downs call **display-mode** standard
  screens/FMs only.
- **Standard objects only** for data sources — standard tables and standard read
  FMs. No custom Z-tables or direct external-system access as a data source.
- **Bounded queries.** Every `SELECT` is constrained by the selection-screen
  period (default −24h). Never full-scan. Name the field list explicitly; avoid
  `SELECT *`.

## Naming & structure

- Namespace `Z` (or the customer namespace). Report `Z_OPS_MONITOR`,
  transaction/message class `ZOPSMON`.
- Interface-first, OO design: `ZIF_MON_DATA_PROVIDER` contract implemented by
  per-area providers (`ZCL_MON_DP_BATCH/DUMP/INTERFACE`); orchestrated by
  `ZCL_MON_CONTROLLER`; UI in `ZCL_MON_UI_DASHBOARD`; drill-down isolated in
  `ZCL_MON_NAVIGATOR`; chart aggregation in `ZCL_MON_AGGREGATOR`.
- Variable prefixes per customer ABAP guide: local `l*`, global `g*`, importing
  `i*`/`im_`, exporting `e*`/`ex_`, members `m*`, constants `c_*`, types `ty_*`.
- New monitoring area = new provider class implementing `ZIF_MON_DATA_PROVIDER`
  + registry entry. Do not touch the controller/UL orchestration to add an area.

## Quality baseline

- All user-facing text via **text symbols** and a **message class** (i18n).
- Thresholds/tunables as **class constants**, not hardcoded literals in logic.
- Per-area isolation: one area's failure (auth/exception/no data) must not break
  others — wrap area calls in `TRY/CATCH` and check authority per area, skipping
  areas the user lacks rights for.
- Keep the design doc in `docs/design/` in sync with code decisions; record open
  questions as `Open Issues` with a `TODO:` marker in code where unresolved.

## Language

- Repository docs and commit messages follow the existing style (Korean design
  docs, Conventional-Commit-style prefixes: `docs:`, `feat:`, `fix:`,
  `refactor:`). Match the surrounding language of the file you edit.
